{title: O Zion, Haste}
{artist: Mary A. Thomson / James Walch}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 130}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Inter-Church Hymnal, compiled by Frank A. Morgan (Chicago, Illinois: Biglow-Main-Excell Company, 1940), # 145)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]O Zion, haste, thy mission [E7]high fulfill[F#m]ing,
[D]To [E7]tell [D]to [A]all the [E7]world that God is [A]light,
[A]That He who made all [C#7]nations is not will[F#m]ing
[B7]One [E]soul should per[C#m]ish, [A]lost in [B]shades of [E7]night.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[E7]Pub[D]lish [E7]glad [A]tidings, [E7]tid[D]ings [E7]of [A7]peace;
[F#7]Tidings of [Bm]Je[D]sus, re[A]demp[E7]tion and re[A]lease.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Behold how many thousands [E7]still are ly[F#m]ing
[D]Bound [E7]in [D]the [A]darksome [E7]prison house of [A]sin,
[A]With none to tell them [C#7]of the Savior’s dy[F#m]ing,
[B7]Or [E]of the life [C#m]He [A]died for [B]them to [E7]win.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Proclaim to every people, [E7]tongue, and na[F#m]tion
[D]That [E7]God, [D]in [A]whom they [E7]live and move, is [A]love;
[A]Tell how He stooped to [C#7]save His lost crea[F#m]tion,
[B7]And [E]died on earth [C#m]that [A]we might [B]live a[E7]bove.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]Give of thy sons to bear the [E7]message glor[F#m]ious;
[D]Give [E7]of [D]thy [A]wealth to [E7]speed them on their [A]way;
[A]Pour out thy soul for [C#7]them in prayer victor[F#m]ious;
[B7]O [E]Zion, haste [C#m]to [A]bring the [B]brighter [E7]day.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
